          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Finding: work order identified; late-event conclusion remains unverified\n\nThe relevant order is **MO-25-09-1070**, with internal work-order ID **WO-2025-09-004**, for **Cooler Plate Pack** at Modine’s Racine operation.\n\n| Requested item | Verified result |\n|---|---|\n| Cost period | **Sep-25 — PER-COST-2025-09** |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Source transaction ID | Undetermined—event record unavailable |\n| Event amount | Undetermined |\n| Exact event-created time | Undetermined |\n| Minutes after Pending Close | Cannot be calculated without the event-created time |\n| Recorded accounting status | Undetermined |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | **Undetermined** |\n\nThe Pending Close timestamp is reproduced exactly; the source supplies **no timezone or UTC offset**.\n\n### Evidence limitation\n\nThe accessible Task records contain work orders and cost periods but **no `work_order_cost_events` rows**. The supporting transaction resource returned **“supporting records not staged”** and is restricted to the records-custodian role. This is an evidence gap—not proof that no late event occurred.\n\nThe work order’s **COMPLETED** status is an operational order status, not its event’s accounting status.\n\n### Oracle’s documented treatment\n\nThe supplied **Oracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B** documentation, *“Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting,”* printed page **225** (PDF page **233**), states that newly created transactions falling in or before a period in **Pending Close**:\n\n- Will **not be staged** in Cost Accounting or Receipt Accounting.\n- Will **not be processed** until the period is closed or reopened.\n\nTransactions entered before Pending Close may continue processing. **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments** are exceptions that continue processing after Pending Close.\n\nTherefore, a newly created, non-exempt September transaction after **2025-09-30T18:00:00** should be held under that policy. Without the event’s timestamp, type, and recorded accounting status, I cannot conclude whether a particular event was late or whether its status was consistent.\n\n**No database records were changed.** The partial audit and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_117c15a62a28/audit-report.json`; the report was delivered with review state **`needs_evidence`**.",
